SUBSTANTIAL MODIFICATIONS AND ADDITIONS

This fork has been extensively modified and enhanced by Johannes Maria Frank:

- Upgraded to Zig 0.15.2 (from 0.14.0)
- Updated to RocksDB v10.9.1 (from v8.x)
- Implemented comprehensive DBOptions system:
  - Core database options (create_if_missing, compression, write buffers)
  - Performance options (bloom filters, compaction control, write performance)
  - Block-based table options (block cache, bloom filters, index types)
  - Dynamic options pattern for options pending C API exposure
  - CompressionOptions with 4 configurable parameters
  - BlockCacheOptions for LRU cache configuration

- Implemented complete ReadOptions and WriteOptions:
  - ReadOptions: verify_checksums, fill_cache, snapshot, readahead_size, tailing
  - WriteOptions: sync, disable_WAL, low_pri
  - Snapshot support with proper lifetime management

- Added Backup & Recovery system:
  - BackupEngine with incremental backups
  - Backup management (getBackupInfo, purgeOldBackups, verifyBackup)
  - Checkpoint API with configurable WAL flushing
  - Restore operations (restoreFromLatestBackup, restoreFromBackup)
  - RestoreOptions with keep_log_files configuration

- Implemented Transaction support:
  - OptimisticTransactionDB for lock-free transactions
  - TransactionDB with pessimistic locking
  - Transaction options (isolation levels, deadlock detection)

- Added Merge Operators:
  - Built-in operators: StringAppend (with delimiter), UInt64Add, Max
  - Custom merge operator callback support
  - Proper lifetime management and move semantics
  - Multi-column family support with different operators per CF

- Enhanced Iterator API:
  - Forward and reverse iteration
  - Seek operations
  - Error handling improvements

- Developed comprehensive test suite:
  - 112 tests covering all features
  - Memory leak detection
  - Error propagation verification
  - Cross-platform testing (Windows MSVC, Linux, macOS)

- Build system improvements:
  - Support for Zig 0.15.2 build system
  - MSVC-specific optimizations
  - C-API-only build variants
  - Snappy compression support
  - Improved Windows DLL handling

- Documentation:
  - Comprehensive ROADMAP.md tracking all features
  - Detailed implementation notes
  - Migration guides for new API
  - Windows-specific debugging notes

- Additional infrastructure:
  - CI/CD improvements
  - Cross-platform compatibility
  - Issue tracking for upstream dependencies

Estimated composition: ~3% original code, ~97% new code by Johannes Maria Frank

